  description:
  - The mass of a Wraith is almost entirely made up of dense low temperature gases.
    Any liquid or wet solid that pass through their gaseous membrane freezes within
    seconds. Fire has been shown to dispel Wraiths, but only temporarily.
  - Additionally, every reported Wraith sighting has involved the presence of an
    almost transparent flower, indicating some form of correlation.
  leftText: 
  rightText: The biomass of a wisp consists of highly concentrated mist fumes, chilled
    to a freezing temperature. It is unknown what actual pilots this being, as no
    organ resembling a brain or a nucleus can be found. A notable trait is the ability
    for the Wisp to phase in and out of a corporeal form at will. This behavior can
    be involuntarily triggered by exposure to flame.
